    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#Switchgear"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A circuit breaker is a safety device to prevent damage to devices in a circuit, such as electric motors, and wiring when the current flowing through the electrical circuit supersedes its design limits. It does this by removing the current from a circuit when an unsafe condition arises. Unlike a switch, a circuit breaker automatically does this and shuts off the power immediately.</skos:definition>
